<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">03072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Russia struck Kyiv overnight with seventy-four missiles and nearly five hundred drones, killing at least twenty-seven people and wounding ninety-one — the deadliest single attack on Ukraine's capital this year.</s> <s>Ukraine's interceptors are faltering as its stock of Patriot missiles runs low, and Moscow called the barrage retaliation.</s> <s>Kyiv's mayor has declared Friday a day of mourning as rescuers still dig through the rubble.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Venezuela's acting president says nearly every local official in La Guaira died when last month's earthquake struck the coastal state hardest.</s> <s>Delcy Rodríguez counts more than eight hundred fifty buildings damaged, a hundred twenty-seven destroyed, and over eight hundred aftershocks since the twenty-fourth of June.</s> <s>A disaster that erases an entire tier of government leaves reconstruction to a state whose local administrators no longer exist.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A bomb hidden under a table killed at least nine lawyers and clerks at a cafe a hundred meters from Syria's Palace of Justice in Damascus.</s> <s>That court is where the new government is trying former officials of the Assad era, and as many as ten thousand former regime loyalists remain at large.</s> <s>No group has claimed the attack, the first serious test of whether the post-Assad state can hold its own capital.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Drone strikes have knocked out the power in El Obeid, the Darfur-to-Nile hinge now besieged by Sudan's Rapid Support Forces.</s> <s>Armed through networks in the United Arab Emirates that Washington itself has sanctioned, the same force killed six thousand people in El Fasher.</s> <s>American officials warn that fresh atrocities loom, yet the world's attention stays elsewhere.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Tehran, workers plant flowers beneath black flags of mourning as Ayatollah Ali Khamenei's body lies in state at the Grand Mosalla.</s> <s>Authorities expect fifteen to twenty million mourners nationwide while clerics quietly weigh who succeeds a man who ruled for more than three decades.</s> <s>Parliament's speaker urges mass turnout and speaks of vengeance, but the question of succession hangs unresolved.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Beijing has issued a legal opinion claiming the entire seabed around Taiwan as Chinese territory.</s> <s>The argument extends China's sovereignty claim to the island's exclusive economic zone, recasting maritime talks between Japan and the Philippines there as an intrusion.</s> <s>It sets a precedent Beijing can invoke well beyond Taiwan's shores.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Narendra Modi will become the first Indian premier to visit New Zealand in forty years when he lands in Auckland on the tenth of July.</s> <s>The trip cashes in an April free trade agreement that removes tariffs on ninety-five percent of New Zealand's exports to India, a rare full opening for a mid-sized economy.</s> <s>Both sides are betting a South-Pacific trade axis can route around the usual poles of Washington and Beijing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Italy is returning to Southeast Asia, but this time through weapons rather than aid.</s> <s>Rome's renewed push runs on defense diplomacy — arms contracts, not the trade deals or development assistance of its past.</s> <s>How far those contracts will reach across the region is still an open question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The American economy added just fifty-seven thousand jobs in June, a sharp slowdown.</s> <s>Leisure and hospitality shed sixty-one thousand positions despite World Cup crowds, while seven hundred thousand people quit the labor force altogether, masking how weak the hiring really was.</s> <s>One economist called it good news for the wrong reasons, reopening the Federal Reserve's debate over cutting rates.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In Santa Marta, Colombia, eighty scientists in four working groups have launched a new panel to chart the world's exit from fossil fuels.</s> <s>Colombia hosted the launch and recruited co-chairs from Brazil, Germany and Cameroon, a Global South body racing to deliver credible advice before COP31.</s> <s>Who gets to define the science of phasing out fossil fuels, and whether this panel can carry the authority of an IPCC, is now the open question.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The first patient has enrolled in a live-outbreak drug trial in the Democratic Republic of Congo, where no approved treatment exists for the Bundibugyo strain of Ebola.</s> <s>The World Health Organization confirms fourteen hundred cases and four hundred thirty-eight deaths so far.</s> <s>Researchers from Oxford, Belgium and Congo are running the trial as the outbreak still spreads.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Health officials have declared an unusual outbreak over after forty-two days without a single new case.</s> <s>The cruise ship Hondius carried thirteen infections and three deaths from a rare hantavirus, and the recommended quarantine period was waited out in full before the all-clear.</s> <s>Researchers across twenty-one countries are now studying how a virus that normally spreads from rodents moved from person to person.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>As Pakistan's monsoon arrives, people living with HIV face a specific danger, and one couple waded through neck-deep water just to save their antiretroviral pills.</s> <s>Last year's floods killed more than a thousand people and displaced three million, and any break in treatment breeds drug resistance and death.</s> <s>Climate disaster doesn't only drown; it severs the medical supply chains that keep chronic patients alive.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Sony will stop producing physical discs for new PlayStation games from January twenty twenty-eight, pushing the largest console platform toward download-only.</s> <s>When a game exists only as a license on a company's servers, players can't resell, lend or preserve it, and publishers can revoke or delist titles at will.</s> <s>Older games stay on disc, but the console front of the shift from owning to renting has now arrived.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Max Schrems is preparing to sue over transatlantic data transfers for a third time, from his group's base in Austria.</s> <s>His challenge targets the legal basis that lets American firms handle Europeans' data, following two earlier cases that already toppled such agreements.</s> <s>A win would void the current Data Privacy Framework and disrupt cloud and software transfers across the industry.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Britain has shelved its National Cyber Action Plan, due Monday, as the governing Labour Party's leadership contest freezes policy.</s> <s>National cybersecurity is time-sensitive infrastructure work, and a domestic political crisis has left critical-systems defense in limbo precisely as state-linked intrusions rise across Europe.</s> <s>That leadership contest opens on the ninth of July, with no new timeline set.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>